From: nabu port
Subject: [PATCH 0001] DarwinBoot 5243c68: keep PA and VA congruent modulo 32 MiB

AllocateWindow placed the kernel so that (PA - VA) is a multiple of 2 MiB.
XNU's start.s builds its bootstrap mappings from L2 blocks and rounds the
virtual and the physical base down independently; with 16 KiB pages an L2
block is 32 MiB. The NABU kernel (16 KiB pages, VA base 0xfffffe0007004000)
loaded at PA 0x48004000 under QEMU virt then mapped every kernel address
16 MiB too high (gva2gpa 0xfffffe0007004000 -> 0x49004000 while the image is
at 0x48004000), and the first instruction of arm_init faulted as undefined.
A 32 MiB block keeps both 4 KiB (2 MiB blocks) and 16 KiB kernels correct.
---
diff --git a/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.c b/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.c
index f0f7650..3e1f8ae 100644
--- a/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.c
+++ b/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.c
@@ -22,7 +22,10 @@
 #include "LoaderInputs.h"
 
 #define WINDOW_SIZE  SIZE_256MB
-#define BLOCK_SIZE   SIZE_2MB
+// Physical placement keeps (PA - VA) a multiple of BLOCK_SIZE. XNU builds its
+// bootstrap mappings from L2 blocks: 2 MiB with 4 KiB pages, 32 MiB with 16 KiB
+// pages (nabu). 32 MiB satisfies both.
+#define BLOCK_SIZE   SIZE_32MB
 // The largest kernel file read: the default window. A macOS kernel collection is about 137 MiB; the window check
 // below still bounds the kernel with everything placed after it.
 #define KERNEL_LIMIT SIZE_256MB
